# tools = Function or first or second; tools("text")
# The variable holds more than the analysis follows in one set, so the untracked object stands for the two functions. It never stands for an evaluator: the set that is given up still lists `Function`,
# so the call is a call of it, and the record names the built-in. call-of-the-untracked-object-is-no-call-of-an-evaluator.ir has the call without the evaluator in the variable
# OPTIONS: limit=MaxValueFlowSetMembers:2
# STATISTIC: MaxValueFlowSetMembersHits >= 1
# RUN: valueflow-solve unseen
# CHECK: unseen EvaluatesText Function
# CHECK: unseen-code yes
# RUN(LOST): valueflow-why lost-builtin=Function lost=f1
# LOST: lost-builtin=Function
# LOST-NEXT: not held
# LOST-NEXT: lost=f1
# LOST-NEXT: n1 lost
# RUN(UNREACHED): valueflow-solve unreached
# UNREACHED-NOT: unreached f1
# UNREACHED-NOT: unreached f2

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
variable g0 name="tools" module=m0 declared={type=anything} initialization=Undefined
function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = NewClosure function=f1
    v1 = NewClosure function=f2
    v2 = Builtin builtin=Function
    PutModuleVariable v2 variable=g0
    PutModuleVariable v0 variable=g0
    PutModuleVariable v1 variable=g0
    v6 = GetModuleVariable variable=g0
    v7 = String string="text"
    v8 = Call v6, -, v7
    Return
}
function f1 name="first" results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    Return
}
function f2 name="second" results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    Return
}
